  "summary": [
    "Batch B, family B2 (`internal_vertices`). Six conjecture-local helpers now unfold to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_interior x y s`, the vertices of a raw sequence `s` other than the given endpoints `x` and `y` (`seq_vertices s :\\: [set x; y]`), the raw-sequence counterpart of coq-graph-theory's `interior` of a packaged path (`seq_interior_nodes`, `seq_interior_val`). X157 (`[set z | z \\in p] :\\: [set x; y]`), X67 and the head-plus-tail X2 (`seq_interior (branch u) (branch v) (branch u :: s)`) are convertible; X175 (head-plus-tail, `seq_interior x y (x :: p)`) and XE2 are boolean comprehensions, extensionally equal through `in_seq_interior`. X172 removes the sequence's own first and last values and gives `set0` on the empty sequence: it unfolds to `GTBase.walks_paths.seq_inner`, equal by `in_seq_inner`. Endpoints are removed as values in every source; positional variants are listed below as distinct.",
    "",
    "Ten statements are affected: X157, X172, X175 and XE2 through their own files, X67, the three X2 rows, and X52 and X90 through X2's `contains_subdivision`. The X157, X172, X175 and XE2 chains are frozen here (helpers in `Legacy`, prefix-dropped chain copies and `statement` in per-row modules; X172 freezes its inductive closure `generated_by_bridge_replacement` with both constructors). The X2, X52, X90 and X67 rows reuse family B1's frozen copies, which froze the whole chain from `x2_path_vertices` and `x67_path_vertices` upwards at 9e03072 and so already freeze `x2_path_internal` and `x67_internal_vertices`. They are not copied again: this family's thin entry points `Digraph.migration.internal_vertices` and the X67 section of `Minor.migration.internal_vertices` state its helper and row certificates over those bodies (kernel-checked conversions through `seq_interior`); the intermediate chain objects keep B1's registered certificates, and B1's certificates rebuild unchanged.",
    "",
    "Kernel evidence, independent of this textual report: `Print All Dependencies` of the 10 frozen statements contains no live helper or chain declaration of this family and neither `seq_interior` nor `seq_inner`, while each live statement reaches `seq_interior` and its alias (/srv/graph-theory-rocq/coordination/evidence/B2-internal_vertices/print_all_dependencies_summary.txt, with the probe and the full output beside it).",
    "",
    "No statement text, doc block, manifest row or leg state changes (checked below), so the documented discrepancies of the affected rows stay verbatim, including the wave-E4 guards of X2 and X52, X2's LEAST clause and candidate edge e173, X157's QUESTION reading with its retargeted specification, and the solved status of X52 and X67. Explicit later variants, untouched: `x166_internals` removes the target only, `x216_internal` removes positions (it differs from `seq_inner` when an endpoint value repeats inside the path), and `x98_internal`/`x114_internal` are pointwise Prop forms of membership in `seq_interior a b p` inside subdivision-model closures."
  ],
